Here's a very short ttyrec (without explanations this time) about how
to kill a shopkeeper with naught but the following setup:

* Invisibility (not necessary permanent but it needs to last long
enough for you to kill the shk)
* Skilled or better in a pole-weapon skill, with a pole-weapon of that
type (so either skilled lance or skilled polearm)

You need to be invisible for the shk to stay just inside the shop. If
you're only carrying items from his store, he'll come after you when
you hit him.

You also need to be skilled or better in a pole-weapon skill to prevent
him from attacking you with his wands (because you stand at a knight's
move away). If you have MR (or can survive magic missiles and/or
striking) then you can use just about any ranged weapon and he won't
come after you.

Here's the ttyrec (I made this in wizmode only because I had no
character capable of doing this at the moment):

http://sartak.katron.org/nh/safe_shk_killing.ttyrec

Note that the following roles cannot use the pole-weapon technique
because they get neither skilled lance nor skilled polearm:
Archeologist, Barbarian, Healer, Monk, Rogue, or Tourist. You also have
to consider whether skilled poleweapon is worth the skill points.

I'm not really sure who the intended audience for this technique is.
Just throwing it out there.

